        }
      ],
      "key":"identity_surface",
      "label":"Identity surface"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "F8 identity's authored foundation-to-law table distinguishes consequences from owned choices. Instance premises not supplied by commitments: (i) many object kinds with runtime/domain owners; (ii) serialised/readable forms read by people/parsers; (iii) release versions belong to releases, not every object. Premise/standing map: scoped/type/uniqueness P3 independent+i; stability P3 independent and P4b derived from P0/P2; boundaries P3/P6 independent, P5 derived from P0/P6 with P0 open-world premise+i; readability P3/P1 independent+ii; hierarchy P3+i,ii; authority split P3/P6+i; authority conservation P6/P3/P4b; defaults P3/P6; parsing P3/P1+ii; release boundary P3/P6+iii; minimum questions P3/P6; implementation policy P3/P1 independent and P0 recovered. Choice ownership remains with the stated owner: object owner for extra coordinates/kinds/form/visible segments; runtime for its generation/defaults; domain for semantic grammar, overrides and family need; WORLD_MODEL/RF-003 for their refinements; issuing authority for grants/decisions; IDENTITY for hierarchy model, grant fields, seven questions and enduring-repair policy; RELEASE for release forms. Examples add no decisions. Consumer applications add no authority beyond their owning rule.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":47,
          "quote":"This member is material family F8, identity. The table below shows which\nof its rules follow from which premises, in the format of\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law),\nwhich also states the standing of the consequences. Instance premises,\nwhich the commitments do not supply:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":43
        },
        {
          "end_line":95,
          "quote":"Each consumer applies the rule and decides nothing the owning section does\nnot (P2, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/IDENTITY.md#IDENTITY%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":94
        }
      ],
      "key":"identity_foundation_derivation",
      "label":"F8 foundation-to-law derivation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Tier 3 Outcome-Driven Development profile for graph-native product authoring over a declared asset graph. It owns graph-native terms in urn:stdo:bounded-context:graph-native-odd under the selected complete STDO basis, imports listed families by reference and restates none. Its traversal and F_D/F_P/F_H shorthands are distinct from a_c traversal records and functor kinds. Executive, Worker and Reviewer are roles over steps; actor, executor, domain operation and functor kind are distinct coordinates. It owns structural traversal-governance and product-authoring law, not consuming-domain semantics or same-spelled runtime carriers.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":21,
          "quote":"This profile's graph traversal and its F_D, F_P and F_H shorthands are its\nown concepts and are not those records by spelling. The Executive, Worker\nand Reviewer of [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md) are roles, and roles\nare relations over steps in which no role name confers an operation\n([ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#roles-and-delegation)); the actor, the\nexecutor, the domain operation and the functor kind are different\ncoordinates (AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS §5) (P3, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD",
          "start_line":15
        },
        {
          "end_line":60,
          "quote":"This profile owns those concepts in the graph-native bounded context\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:graph-native-odd` under the selected complete\nSTDO basis. The context covers the ODD product shape, the GTL language\nrole, the ABG method role, graph assets, vectors, functions, traversals and\nthe graph and runtime worker and evaluator shorthands defined here. It does\nnot absorb a consuming Product's domain semantics, nor a concrete runtime's\ncarriers that happen to share a spelling (P1, P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position",
