        }
      ],
      "key":"odd_profile",
      "label":"Outcome-Driven Development profile"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "GTL, Graph Transformation Language, is the capability role of a typed declarative graph language and the language expression of ODD. It does not require a particular repository, package, vendor or implementation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":52,
          "quote":"ODD, GTL and ABG name normative capability roles and a construction\nalgebra, not a required repository, package, vendor or concrete\nimplementation. ODD, Outcome-Driven Development, names the graph-native\nproduct-authoring profile. GTL, Graph Transformation Language, names the\nrole of the typed declarative graph language. ABG names the role of the\nsingular traversal-governance and runtime-truth authority (P1, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position",
