      "definition": "FOUNDATIONS P0's bounded step, referenced here as the source of ODD's binding: selected context fits the actor's envelope, internal path belongs to the actor, and traversal supplies admissible external space. Its full foundational definition is not supplied.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":309,
          "quote":"Direction: from the step of\nFOUNDATIONS P0 to one declared ODD vector or edge traversal. Preserved\nmeaning: the step's selected context fits the actor's envelope, the\nactor's internal path within the step is its own, and the traversal is\nthe admissible external space. Narrowed scope: one declared vector or edge\ntraversal of a published graph. Invalidation: a change to FOUNDATIONS P0,\nto the vector's declaration or to the selected basis invalidates the\nbinding until it is evaluated again (P0, P1).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute",
