      "definition": "urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-d: deterministic evaluation or proof over declared traversal properties. It may optimise or validate a domain-local path where the domain makes work precise, without moving domain HOW into GTL, ABG or the framework.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":335,
          "quote":"- `F_D` (`urn:stdo:concept:graph-native-odd:f-d`) is the shorthand for\n  deterministic evaluation or proof over declared properties of the\n  traversal. F_D may optimise or validate a domain-local path where the\n  domain can make part of the work precise; it does not move domain HOW\n  into GTL, ABG or the framework.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FProbabilistic%20compute",
