    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Named constructive program realising a vector: directly, through a small inner workflow refining one outer vector, or as a reusable higher-order library function. The outer vector remains its constitutional callable contract.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":374,
          "quote":"Graph functions are named constructive programs that realise vectors. A\ngraph function may realise one outer vector directly, refine one outer\nvector into a small inner workflow, or act as a reusable higher-order\nlibrary function. The outer vector remains the constitutional contract;\nthe graph function is the constructive realisation of that contract (P4a,\nP0).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions",
