    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Referenced ACTIVATION §4 typed refinement allows earlier outputs to reach later steps only through a declared adapter or specialised contract whose declared domain names them. ODD binds it to a graph function refining one outer vector; the full general law is external.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":382,
          "quote":"[ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement) generalises the\nrefinement of one outer vector into an inner workflow to any realisation,\nlets a refinement carry an earlier output to a later step only through a\ndeclared adapter or specialised contract whose declared domain names it,\nand names [PROFILES §2](PROFILES.md#2-graph-execution), which indexes this\nprofile, as the keeper of the ODD binding.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions",
