    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "ODD §11.8's specialised cumulative carried environment, conserved as profile law rather than generalised into the core. A later function's declared domain is environment.requires and may require any typed binding available in the cumulative environment, not only the preceding output. Retained functions should declare environment.requires, environment.provides and environment.carries.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":397,
          "quote":"Narrowed scope: one published outer\nvector and its declared inner workflow, whose retained functions should\ndeclare `environment.requires`, `environment.provides` and\n`environment.carries` (§11.8); a later function's declared domain is its\n`environment.requires`, which may require any typed binding available in\nthe cumulative carried environment, not only the immediately previous\noutput.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F5.%20Graph%20model%2FGraph%20functions",
          "start_line":391
        }
