      "key":"cumulative_carried_environment",
      "label":"Cumulative carried environment"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The mutable source library authors a future method release; consumers select one complete immutable release distributed in the shared versioned STDO store. Both libraries contain method members, guides and templates. Only README-designated method members—tier 1, tier 2 and selected tier 3 profiles—are constitutional method surfaces. *_GUIDE.md documents refine application; *_TEMPLATE.md files are reusable starter forms/examples and convenience artifacts only.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":269,
          "quote":"Both the authoring library and an installed distribution contain three\nclasses of document. Method members are the constitutional method\nsurfaces, the members that [README](README.md#documents) names as method\nmembers: the tier 1 and tier 2 standards and, when a\nproject selects them, the tier 3 profiles. Guides (`*_GUIDE.md`) are operational guides and application standards\nthat refine application of the method. Templates (`*_TEMPLATE.md`) are\nreusable starter forms and examples and are convenience artifacts only.\nOnly method members are constitutional method surfaces (P6, P3).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F4.%20Method%20library%20classes",
          "start_line":262
        }
      ],
      "key":"method_library",
      "label":"Method library and document classes"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The installed graph-native product supplies the method, runtime and carrier surfaces, owning traversal-control substrate, runtime/control/command surfaces, release-managed methodology and scaffold templates. It is distinct from the target project and, in self-hosting, from the next version under development.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":424,
          "quote":"The installed product owns the graph-native method and its\ntraversal-control substrate, the runtime and control surfaces, the command\nsurfaces, the release-managed methodology surfaces and the project\nscaffold templates (P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary",
