    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The project built with an installed ODD product owns its business domain; one stdo_<label>.json definition per distinct product WHAT locating constitutional, local/collective reference-frame basis, realisation, work and composition surfaces; constitutional surfaces; one or more how.build_tenants realisation roots; domain outputs and evidence. Software examples include design, code, tests, documents and proof surfaces; other domains name their own artifacts.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":438,
          "quote":"- one `stdo_<label>.json` definition for each distinct product WHAT,\n  locating its constitutional, local and collective reference-frame\n  basis, realisation, work and composition surfaces;\n- its constitutional surfaces under SPEC_METHOD, where `GOALS.md`,\n  `INTENT.md`, `PRODUCT.md` and `requirements/` are the default\n  software-development scaffold and not mandatory names;\n- one or more realisation roots bound through `how.build_tenants`, where\n  `build_tenants/` is the default root name for software-development ODD\n  products and existing projects and other domain types may use their own\n  locations;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F6.%20Product%20boundary",
