      "conditions": ["A product is built with the ODD profile."],
      "definition": "F18's authored foundation-to-law table imports F1 frames/context, F2 transitions/steps/configuration, F3 results, F4 work-state/resumption/reuse, F6 claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance, F9 a_c, F10 constitutional chain/outcome/build tenants, F11 change/ambiguity, F12 project binding, F13 work carriers and F15 release/successor conservation; rules and choices retain their owners. Adopted instance premises, not foundational deductions: I1 externally admitted selected Product outcome; I2 mutable workspace beside immutable ledger/event log; I3 bounded probabilistic workers whose reports/artifacts are observations; I4 installed method-product release, possibly an earlier self release. The 25 rows distinguish derived consequences from profile/product/consumer/other-member choices. Standing includes P0 recovered; P1/P2/P3/P4a/P6 independent; P4b derived from P0/P2; P5 derived from P0/P6. Consumer applications decide nothing beyond rule owners. §1's opening, §16 failure patterns, §19 checklist and §20 compression add no independent law; §11 decides built correctness and §9 move compliance.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
