    {
      "applies_to_keys":["odd_profile","odd_domain_product","abg_runtime_role"],
      "conditions":["A product is claimed to be built using ODD."],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":45,
          "quote":"ODD is a programming paradigm, not only a documentation preference. Its form\nis `product = typed asset/domain model + GTL-defined graph functions + ABG\ntraversal-control runtime + governed projection/query surfaces`. A product\nwhose constructive carrier stays hidden in imperative loops, local service\nlogic or product-specific orchestration scripts is not yet built with this\nprofile (P0, P6).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F1.%20Position",
          "start_line":40
        }
      ],
      "key":"odd_construction_shape",
      "statement":"Using ODD means building a GTL/ABG domain product with typed assets/nodes, named published graph functions bound into a GTL module, ABG-owned traversal governance/runtime facts/provenance/continuation/re-entry, bounded cooperative commands/services returning evidence and control, and visible state projected over constructive history. Documents, graph sketches or helper scripts alone do not satisfy that meaning; a hidden imperative constructive carrier leaves it not yet built with the profile. Automation must remain within lawful manual traversal of the same graph.",
      "uncertainty":""
    },
