          "start_line":209
        },
        {
          "end_line":237,
          "quote":"An agent that reads only this profile should understand the paradigm.\nTo build one concrete product correctly it must then read the\nproduct-specific method and the local authority surfaces (P1, P2).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F3.%20Method%20composition",
          "start_line":235
        }
      ],
      "key":"odd_method_composition_requirements",
      "statement":"SPEC_METHOD supplies general constitutional goals/intent/product/requirements/design/re-entry law. ODD supplies graph-native structure and product shape, not domain semantics or the current local line. Domain methods supply semantic law; local INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md, requirements and design supply the ratified local line, with GTL surfaces included for graph-native software development. When WORLD_MODEL is also adopted, it governs world-model semantics, publication and composition. A source-described builder must acquire the product-specific method and local authority surfaces to build correctly; ODD alone is insufficient.",
      "uncertainty":"The referenced general/domain methods and actual product surfaces are not supplied."
