      "key":"abg_continuation_exclusivity",
      "statement":"The application is cooperative, not a replacement runtime. ABG owns continuation, publish-boundary re-entry, graph-call lifecycle and graph step selection. Product code must not hold hidden continuation loops, multi-step controller memory across publish boundaries, locally infer later steps instead of ABG re-entry, make public next and graph-function continuation rival authorities, or otherwise replace ABG orchestration. Replacing ABG continuation with tenant-local flow leaves the application outside ODD-over-GTL/ABG behaviour.",
      "uncertainty":""
    },
