      "statement":"Inventory at least all five authority surfaces. ABG owns selection/advance; invocation/supervision; retry/correction/continuation/re-entry; runtime events/append/replay/projection; and closure/assurance, with product policy/gain inputs. Product/plugin roles are declarations and policy inputs, actor bindings/prompts/payload/evidence adapters, bounded outputs and control return, admitted evidence payload mapping, and domain interpretation/evaluators/gap reasons/weights. Forbidden local substitutes include next-step runners; spawn/spawnSync/exec/timeout/kill/stdout-stderr supervision outside the ABG seam; retries/controller memory/hidden next; direct event append/side-ledger mutation/bypassing reconstruction; self-report or postflight closure. Include language/tenant-appropriate code, call-graph or static-surface review and name evidence ruling out hidden execution authority; artifact review alone is insufficient.",
