      "key":"foundation_table_additional_proof_obligations",
      "statement":"Every automated move must be possible for an actor holding only declared surfaces; agentic artifacts take effect only through admission against deterministic criteria, and conformance evidence is not ratification. Negative evidence invalidates the real authority-bearing input on the supported path and demonstrates refusal before prohibited effect; manufactured refusal/event/gap/verdict proves nothing about that path, and source/package/install/runtime absence are distinct claims. Decisive proof uses an installable development form where one exists; isolation/proving-lane provisions remain recommendations. Refined inner chains close enclosing carriers only if outer contract survives fold-back and zoomed/unzoomed views agree. A live requirement without a proof witness keeps the enclosing carrier open until realised or owner-deferred/repriced out of the active branch. Scenario bundles should clarify boundary, assets, vectors, paths and closure evidence; products choose scenarios and appropriate witnesses.",
